# SRG-APP-000092-AU-000670  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must initiate session auditing upon startup.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000092-AU-000670
group:           V-221907
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-001464
control_rev5:    AU-14

contribution:    Splunk's audit trail is generated by splunkd from the moment it starts and
                 has no enable switch. What the application configures is whether those
                 audit events are routed into the index queue as they are generated
                 (audit.conf [auditTrail] queueing), so the session records are searchable
                 from startup rather than only written to the audit log file.

governs:         audit.conf - The audit trail Splunk keeps of its own activity, and how those records
                 are signed.

check:           audit.conf [auditTrail] queueing not_equals false

external:        The operating system's service manager must start splunkd at boot (a
                 systemd unit or Splunk boot-start), which determines when auditing
                 actually begins; "upon startup" is bounded by that and is not an
                 application setting.
external:        If queueing is deliberately set to false, the compensating inputs.conf
                 stanza that tails the audit log is the assessable alternative; that is a
                 separate input definition rather than a value of this key.

citation:        SRG-APP-000092-AU-000670 check text; audit.conf.spec:23-29 ([auditTrail],
                 queueing = <boolean>, "If set to false, you must add an inputs.conf stanza
                 to tail the audit log", Default: true); audit.conf.spec:6-8 (there is no
                 default audit.conf; custom settings are placed in a local audit.conf)
finding:         audit.conf [auditTrail] queueing is set to false and no input tails the
                 audit log, so the session audit events splunkd generates at startup do not
                 reach an index.
